\nDo not expand methodology.\n\nDo not redesign the system.\n\nYour task is to convert the accepted Gate 6 rulings into a clean implementation-facing handoff that I can upload directly into Kimi's desktop/runtime.\n\nCREATE ONE PRIMARY FILE:\n\n`EC8_ECQ_GATE7_KIMI_IMPLEMENTATION_HANDOFF_2026-09-22.md`\n\nThe file must be self-contained enough for Kimi to execute Gate 7 without having to reinterpret the architecture review.\n\nSTRUCTURE\n\n# 1. AUTHORITY / STATUS\n\nState clearly:\n\n- Gate 5 technical methodology: ACCEPTED\n- Gate 6 material architecture: PROCEED\n- Gate 7 Design & Build: AUTHORIZED\n- Parent Quant remains sport-agnostic\n- No sport-specific methodology may be invented during build\n- Kimi owns implementation choices inside the architecture boundaries below\n\n# 2. BINDING ARCHITECTURE RULINGS\n\nExtract only the architecture decisions that Kimi must treat as binding.\n\nInclude at minimum:\n\n- modular monolith / one deployable unless later architecture evidence requires otherwise\n- eight logical architecture boundaries\n- event-sourced bitemporal append-only log as system of record\n- relational authoritative state + object storage boundary\n- immutable Baseline\n- separate Don Delta\n- separate Model Synthesis\n- append-only / supersession semantics\n- contract-scoped write authority\n- deterministic replay requirements\n- persisted computed-state derivation/version identity\n- injected clock requirement\n- ordered deterministic hashing\n- fixed-point / deterministic numeric behavior where already ruled\n- sport-module trust boundary\n- source/license-policy-driven retention\n- retention/purge actions as first-class auditable events\n- explicit replay-gap behavior\n- credential/secrets boundary\n- audit/observability trace requirements\n- as_of_knowledge_time requirements\n- failure-domain rules\n- hard-stop vs certification-block vs degraded behavior\n\nDo not restate explanatory prose unless it is needed to implement the ruling.\n\n# 3. REQUIR