ntity\n- as_of_event_time\n- as_of_knowledge_time\n- Don Delta version if present\n- synthesis version if present\n- clock source\n- ordered input-set hash\n- runtime/build version\n- output/state hash\n\nState:\n\nSame authoritative inputs + same versions + same declared configuration must reproduce the same authoritative state.\n\nReplay divergence is a certification failure, not an acceptable variance.\n\n# 7. FAILURE BEHAVIOR\n\nTranslate the Gate 6 failure model into build requirements.\n\nIdentify:\n\nHARD STOP\n\n- version incompatibility\n- look-ahead / knowledge-time violation\n- license violation\n- forbidden mutation / authority breach\n- any architecture-defined trust-boundary breach\n\nCERTIFICATION BLOCK\n\n- deterministic replay divergence\n- state cannot be fully audited\n- lineage/provenance chain is incomplete where required\n\nLOUD DEGRADATION\n\n- missing source\n- stale source\n- proxy substitution\n- unavailable optional evidence\n- market feed degradation\n- product/API availability problems that do not invalidate analytical state\n\nPreserve:\n\nMISSING != ZERO\\\nPROXY != DIRECT\\\nDATA PRIORITY != MODEL WEIGHT\n\n# 8. SECURITY / LICENSE ENFORCEMENT\n\nGive Kimi implementation requirements for:\n\n- secrets referenced by logical names, not embedded\n- credential isolation\n- write-authority enforcement\n- baseline mutation denial\n- privileged action audit\n- source-license metadata\n- retention-policy attachment\n- raw / normalized / derived / cache / snapshot / export retention behavior\n- explicit purge logging\n- no assumption that derived data may always be retained\n\nDo not choose a vendor unless architecture already requires one.\n\n# 9. IMPLEMENTATION CHOICES RETURNED TO KIMI\n\nExplicitly list what Chiave is NOT deciding and Kimi may choose during Gate 7.\n\nInclude:\n\n- programming language\n- framework\n- database engine, provided architecture invariants hold\n- serialization format\n- API style\n- repository layout\n- module/pa