ccessor MLB manifest design;\n- canonical `ecq-synthesis-v1` registration;\n- multiple architecture gates around synthesis;\n- a new FixedDec value contract;\n- exhaustive cross-seat certification of every later layer.\n\nThose entered later.\n\n---\n\n# B. EXPECTED SIZE OF WORK\n\n### Classification: **NORMAL BUILD**\n\nIt was larger than bounded maintenance because there was no current React web surface on disk and a new vertical slice had to be assembled.\n\nIt was **not initially an architecture-change request** because Gate 6 architecture and Parent Quant methodology already existed and the intended first pass explicitly fit inside them.\n\nA sane estimate of the original work shape was:\n\n**inspect existing repo → build adapter/contracts/API projection → React view → tests → show Don.**\n\nThe first slice legitimately required engineering discipline, but it did **not** require repeated governance expansion.\n\n---\n\n# C. ACTUAL WORK PERFORMED\n\nOnly concrete built/tested outcomes are counted here.\n\n### 1. React DevPad / Baseline slice — genuinely built\n\nA Vite/React/TypeScript DevPad was created over the frozen MLB fixture.\n\nIt materially provided:\n\n- 12-game MLB PREGAME slate;\n- event selection;\n- separate BASELINE view;\n- component/evidence drill-down;\n- provenance;\n- uncertainty/evidence state;\n- generic sport-module boundary;\n- immutable Baseline;\n- deterministic state identity;\n- injected clock;\n- read-only enforcement.\n\nThis was a **real visible product outcome**.\n\n### 2. SHA-256 defect — genuinely found and fixed\n\nInitial implementation contained a broken custom SHA-256 padding calculation.\n\nLuce correctly found that hashes labeled SHA-256 did not match standards.\n\nNico/Big Pickle then actually repaired:\n\n- SHA-256 padding;\n- fixed-vector tests;\n- Node crypto cross-checks;\n- derived state identity;\n- browser compatibility;\n- app→test dependency.\n\nResult reached:\n\n**37/37 tests + clean build.**\n\nThis was valid corrective work.\n\n### 3. Don Delta — genuinely built\n\nA second independently addressable view was implemented:\n\n**Human input → classification → validation → Don Delta.**\n\nActual implementation included:\n\n- immutable human input records;\n- classification surface;\n- validation state;\n- append-only Don Delta ledger;\n- supersession;\n- write authority;\n- anti-lookahead;\n- deterministic replay;\n- React Don Delta UI;\n- three-view routing.\n\nResult eventually reached:\n\n**73/73 tests.**\n\n### 4. Clock/vocabulary repair — genuinely implemented\n\nThe Don Delta implementation was revised so that:\n\n- `RunClock` pinned a declared run instant;\n- authoritative writes stopped depending on accidental execution-time variance;\n- validation became:\n  `UNVALIDATED / VALIDATED / REFUTED / EXPIRED`;\n- verification became the orthogonal:\n  `FULL / PARTIAL / UNVERIFIABLE`;\n- Don Delta envelope was versioned appropriately.\n\nResult reached:\n\n**94/94 tests.**\n\n### 5. Generic Model Synthesis shell — genuinely built\n\nThe third state was materially implemented as generic infrastructure:\n\n- Model Synthesis envelope;\n- deterministic identity;\n- exact Baseline lineage;\n- exact Don Delta lineage;\n- append-only synthesis history;\n- write authority;\n- replay;\n- anti-lookahead;\n- React Model Synthesis view;\n- NON-CANON transcript transform;\n- loud failure when the canonical MLB transform did not exist.\n\nThis was another **real visible product outcome**.\n\nResult reached:\n\n**114/114 tests + clean build.**\n\n### 6. Canonical MLB synthesis math core — genuinely built\n\nCorrado defined enough MLB numeric semantics for Nico to implement a pure math core.\n\nNico actually implemented:\n\n`mlb_ecq_synthesis_v1.ts`\n\nincluding:\n\n- additive `M_delta`;\n- per-variable bounds;\n- ±0.10 total cap;\n- 0.05/0.95 probability clamp;\n- complement conservation;\n- 6dp integer/micro-unit arithmetic;\n- no interactions;\n- lane gating.\n\nTests eventually reached:\n\n**127/127**, then **129/129** after lane-map correction.\n\n### 7. Lane-map defect — genuinely fixed\n\nLuce found:\n\n- MONEYLINE incorrectly admitted weather/park/umpire;\n- TOTALS `days_rest` required a semantic ruling.\n\nCorrado ruled TOTALS excludes `days_rest`.\n\nNico corrected the lane sets and added regression tests.\n\nLuce independently reverified:\n\n- MONEYLINE 5 families;\n- TOTALS 7;\n- RUNLINE 5;\n- 129/129 green.\n\nThis was valid engineering correction.\n\n### 8. Value-materialization architecture — **not yet built**\n\nAt session end, Chiave had frozen a proposed value-materialization contract.\n\nBut the actual new layer was **not yet implemented**.\n\nTherefore it is not a completed deliverable.\n\n---\n\n# D. LOOP ONSET\n\nThere are two useful boundaries.\n\n### Product-scope drift began after the original first slice\n\nOnce the Baseline React DevPad existed and was verified, the original visible outcome had been achieved.\n\nMoving to Don Delta was an **explicitly authorized expansion by Don**, so I would **not** call that alone the loop.\n\n### Actual loop onset: after the generic Model Synthesis shell was working\n\nThe strongest loop onset is when the session moved from:\n\n> **“Model Synthesis shell exists and correctly fails loudly because canonical MLB synthesis semantics are absent.”**\n\nto:\n\n> **“Now let's make canonical `ecq-synthesis-v1@1.0.0` executable inside this same DevPad session.”**\n\nThat decision converted a successful product-build session into a methodology + architecture + contract-reconciliation program.\n\nAt that point the shell itself had already proven the boundary correctly: **SPORT GAP → Corrado**.\n\nInstead of closing the DevPad build at that visible checkpoint, the session continued into:\n\nCorrado semantics → Nico math core → Luce → lane correction → Corrado → Nico → Luce → Chiave → Corrado value materialization → Chiave new contract freeze.\n\nThat is the clearest loop branch.\n\n---\n\n# E. LOOP MECHANISM\n\nThe loop became:\n\n**Don → Coda framing → Nico → Luce → Coda → next layer → Nico → Luce → Coda → specialty seat → Nico → Luce → architecture gate → new contract → next implementation.**\n\nMore specifically:\n\n### Phase 1 — Healthy\n\n**Coda → Nico → Luce**\n\nBaseline React slice.\n\nLuce found a real SHA problem.\n\n**Nico fix → Luce reverify.**\n\nThis was normal build/verify/fix.\n\n### Phase 2 — Still productive, but expanding\n\n**Don authorizes Don Delta → Nico → Luce.**\n\nLuce finds clock/vocabulary issues.\n\nInstead of treating this as one bounded closure patch, orchestration added:\n\n- pre-Slice-3 reconciliation;\n- special Nico grounding;\n- Coda reconciliation;\n- separate repair verification;\n- final Coda reconciliation.\n\nUseful work occurred, but process started expanding around the work.\n\n### Phase 3 — Generic Model Synthesis\n\n**Don → Nico → Luce.**\n\nAgain productive. A visible third view existed.\n\nBut then the shell's intentionally loud missing-transform condition became the next project.\n\n### Phase 4 — Recursive semantic integration\n\n**Coda → Corrado**\ndefines canonical MLB synthesis.\n\nCorrado reports undefined semantics.\n\n**Don/Coda ruling → Nico**\nbuilds math core.\n\n**Luce**\nfinds lane-map issue.\n\n**Corrado**\nrules TOTALS/rest.\n\n**Nico**\npatches.\n\n**Luce**\nreverifies.\n\nAt this point the math core is valid, but still not runnable through the shell.\n\n### Phase 5 — Architecture recursion\n\n**Chiave**\nreviews shell registration.\n\nChiave correctly refuses because the shell has references but there is **no certified producer for numeric delta magnitudes**.\n\nThis is the most important evidence that the session had outrun its original operating frame.\n\nThe missing thing was no longer \"one code fix.\"\n\nIt was:\n\n> **There is no authoritative human-read → quantitative-value layer.**\n\nThen:\n\n**Coda → Corrado**\ndefines value materialization.\n\nCorrado discovers human utterance → numeric