plicitly bounded?\n\nInitially, yes:\n\n**Frozen MLB → React DevPad → one game → Baseline.**\n\nThe boundary degraded as later work was appended.\n\n### Authority clear?\n\nSeat authority was repeatedly stated and usually clear.\n\nIronically, authority clarity did **not** prevent the loop.\n\nIt made routing easier, which allowed the session to keep expanding.\n\n### Expected artifact clear?\n\nFor Slice 1: yes.\n\nFor later stages: increasingly less so.\n\nThe goal drifted from:\n\n**\"make the DevPad work\"**\n\nto:\n\n**\"make canonical MLB Model Synthesis executable under every governing invariant.\"**\n\nThose are materially different jobs.\n\n### Stop condition?\n\nSlice prompts individually had stop conditions.\n\nThe **session as a whole did not**.\n\nThere was no persistent rule like:\n\n> Once the current visible vertical slice is runnable and verified, close the session. New methodology gaps become separate work.\n\n### Session footer/outcome ledger?\n\nIndividual seat handoffs eventually had formal footers.\n\nThe Coda chat did not consistently use one.\n\nThat is important: **the subprocesses were better framed than the parent orchestration.**\n\n### When controls disappeared\n\nThe clearest loss occurs after the generic Model Synthesis shell was verified.\n\nInstead of closing the current implementation session, the next SPORT GAP was consumed into the same conversation.\n\n---\n\n# L. WHAT SHOULD HAVE HAPPENED\n\nWithout changing the architecture, the shortest sane path was:\n\n### Pass 1\n\n**Clear ask**\n\nReact DevPad for frozen MLB Baseline.\n\n### Pass 2\n\n**One coherent build**\n\nAdapter + state + API projection + React + tests.\n\n### Pass 3\n\n**Show Don the runnable artifact**\n\n12 games → event → Baseline → drill-down.\n\n### Pass 4\n\n**One verification checklist**\n\nLuce checks critical invariants.\n\n### Pass 5\n\n**Bounded fixes**\n\nFix SHA and other actual defects.\n\n### Pass 6\n\n**Final verification and close**\n\nAt that point